@startuml
title FR-21 - Generate Demand Forecast - Activity Diagram

|Blood Bank Administrator|
start
:Request a forecast within the permitted blood bank scope;

|Client|
:Display the approved forecasting interface;

|Blood Bank Administrator|
repeat
  :Select the component and ABO/Rh group;
  :Click the generate button;

  |Server — Analytics & AI|
  :Verify permission for the selected blood bank scope;

  if (Bank scope permitted?) then (Yes)
    |Server — Requests|
    :Retrieve historical submitted demand aggregates\nfor the addressed bank, component and ABO/Rh group;

    |Server — Analytics & AI|
    if (Historical demand retrieved successfully?) then (Yes)
      :Prepare historical demand data and assess\nits sufficiency under the approved model policy;

      if (Preparation succeeded and data is sufficient?) then (Yes)
        |AI Service|
        :Run the approved forecasting method\nusing the prepared aggregated history;

        |Server — Analytics & AI|
        :Validate the forecasting outcome;

        if (Processing succeeded and result is valid?) then (Yes)
          :Save a new forecast with its result,\ncomponent, ABO/Rh group, bank scope\nand identifying information;

          if (Complete forecast saved successfully?) then (Yes)
            |Client|
            :Display the saved result or a completion message;
          else (No)
            |Client|
            :Report generation failure;
            stop
          endif

        else (No)
          |Client|
          :Report generation failure;
          stop
        endif

      else (No)
        |Client|
        :Report generation failure and explain\ninsufficient data or preparation failure;
        stop
      endif

    else (No)
      |Client|
      :Report generation failure;
      stop
    endif

  else (No)
    |Client|
    :Explain that the selected bank scope is not permitted;
    stop
  endif

  |Blood Bank Administrator|
repeat while (Generate for another component or group?) is (Yes) not (No)

stop
@enduml